     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risks include GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nCould this be a typo or a mix-up? Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily** or another titration step.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale, which I can add to the order note."
      }
     ],
